   "path": "SCENE.md",
   "role": "instructions",
   "content": "# Glass Code Walk\n\nA camera that scans a frosted-glass code block top to bottom as its lines appear, then pulls back to a centred hold.\n\nCategory: ui-blocks. Length: 5 s. WebGL: no.\n\nUse when:\n- A code reveal needs camera motion: the frame stays pinned to the line currently appearing, then pulls back so the whole file lands as the payoff.\n- The snippet is too small to read at full frame and you want it magnified while it appears.\n\nAvoid when:\n- The code panel should sit still: use glass-code-block.\n- The point is code producing live UI side by side: use live-code-compilation.\n\nVariables:\n- code (string): Code, default \"import { Scene } from \\\"./scene\\\";\\nimport { Typewriter } from \\\"./typewriter\\\";\\n\\nexport function Intro() {\\n  return (\\n    <Scene>\\n      <Typewriter text=\\\"Ship it\\\" />\\n    </Scene>\\n  );\\n}\"\n- title (string): Title, default \"scene.tsx\"\n- width (number, 300-1100): Width, default 880\n- height (number, 200-700): Height, default 420\n- zoom (number, 1-4): Zoom, default 2.6\n- font_size (number, 10-28): Font size, default 18\n- stagger_frames (number, 1-30): Stagger, default 10\n- speed (number, 0.25-4): Speed, default 1\n\nSource: https://github.com/Remocn/remocn. Licence: MIT. The scene file keeps the upstream notice.\n"
  },
